        "bookmarked": false,
        "raw": "The Shaughterlouse Six!\n\nThat bit about never-completed roleplaying sessions really gets me in the feels.  When OblivAeon grants me the terrible burden of power, I'll be using it to travel through time and complete all the plans that have ever been imagined, so that the cosmos can be destroyed in the sense of being totally complete, with nothing else remaining to be done.\n\nThis is like the fifth episode about RPG stuff.  Besides Daybreak, there were also Helfyre, Perestroika and Timeslinger.\n\nAny excuse to have Khatchaturian run through my head is a good one.....\n\nI love the idea that Ray Manta believes the true OblivAeon is Roko's Basilisk.  He probably read IHNMAIMS at a formative age.\n\nAs a huge fan of KVJ, I have great trouble taking the gag about him in stride.\n\nSince the only connection point between the two teams named For Profit is the presence of Heartbreaker, he must have been the one to suggest the team's name.\n\nI'm sure Clockwork Cthulhu create Chaos frequently, but did the Chaos Clockwork create Cthulhu?\n\nI think Glamour must be autistic, because she used to be the (Sh)REEEEiker.  That's  how she got in touch with REEEEvocorp.",
